From 410bba5251687d91bcb259f8f38fb9c6b0a4b17d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: onedoor delivery <delivery@onedoor.local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 23:15:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] ND-024: retire vestigial Sutradhar schema (intake_policy,
 preferences, sessions)

Three tables created by 0001 have never been read by any module under onedoor/.
Dead schema in a governance product is not inert: a reader who opens the database
sees tables implying governed surfaces -- an intake/sensing policy, a preference
store, a session model -- that this engine does not have.

Migrations are forward-only, so 0001 keeps its CREATE statements and the history
stays legible; 0006 drops the tables rather than editing them out of the past.
push_subscriptions is explicitly NOT dropped -- it is unread today but reserved for
ND-026 (web-push delivery), and now says so in a comment.

Tests assert the fresh schema, forward migration from a pre-0006 database, and --
the one that matters -- that the append-only triggers on actions_audit and
policy_versions survive the migration and still bite.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
